>> title: Fresh Egg Pasta
>> category: Pasta
>> tags: pasta, eggs, flour, italian, fresh, tagliatelle
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: pasta all'uovo, pasta alluovo, egg pasta, fresh pasta, tagliatelle, fettuccine, sfoglia
>> pairs-with: bolognese, basil-pesto, alfredo-sauce
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — ninety seconds in the water and fresh pasta is done, where dry would still be raw, and an overcooked ribbon does not come back

>> step: mix to a stiff dough
Mix @00 flour{2%cup}(280 g), @eggs{3%large}(150 g), @egg yolks{2}(30 g), @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp} and @extra-virgin olive oil{1%tsp}(5 mL) to a dough far stiffer than a bread dough — it should be barely damp and hard to bring together.

>> step: knead 10 min, until it springs back
Knead @&(~1)dough{} ~knead{10%min}, leaning into it on an unfloured board, until the surface goes smooth and a poked dent fills back in slowly.

>> step: rest 30 min, wrapped
Rest @&(~1)dough{} wrapped tight ~rest{30%min}, which is what lets a dough this dry roll out at all.

>> step: roll thin and cut in ribbons
Roll @&(~1)rested dough{} in four pieces out to the thickness of a postcard on @semolina{1/4%cup}(40 g), fold the sheets loosely and cut them across into 1/4-in ribbons.

>> step: cook 90 sec, and keep a cup of the water
Boil @&(~1)tagliatelle{} in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) with @kosher salt{2%Tbs} ~cook{90%sec}, until it floats and no longer tastes of raw flour, and lift a cup of the water out with it.

Toss it into the pan of sauce with a splash of that water and keep it moving over the heat for half a minute.
